flowchart LR
    accTitle: From dependency injection to a governed object runtime
    accDescr: A typical dependency injection container emphasizes provider registration, object-graph construction, familiar lifetimes, injection, and scope cleanup. Melder retains that core and adds explicit runtime ownership, validated and gated execution, live topology under change control, mediated access, persistence, restore, and research.

    app["Application code"]

    subgraph di["Typical DI container · common baseline"]
        direction TB
        register["Register providers"]
        resolve["Resolve / inject"]
        object_graph["Construct object graph"]
        lifetime["Singleton · scoped · transient"]
        dispose["Clean the scope"]
        register --> resolve --> object_graph
        lifetime -.-> object_graph
        object_graph --> dispose
    end

    retained["DI core retained<br/>providers · resolution<br/>lifetimes · cleanup"]

    subgraph melder["Melder · Dependency Graph Runtime"]
        direction TB
        bind["Bind definitions + Existence"]
        compile["Validate and compile phases 1–11"]
        world["AethericFrame + Conduits"]
        meld["Gated Meld resolution"]
        objects["Scoped live object world"]
        bind --> compile --> world --> meld --> objects

        runtime["Explicit runtime ownership<br/>frame · conduit · SpellSpace"]
        governance["Validated, gated execution<br/>validity · dirty roots · gates"]
        topology["Live topology under change control<br/>links · clusters · ownership transfer"]
        advanced["Mediated access and continuity<br/>Rift · Crystallizer · Research"]

        world -.-> runtime
        compile -.-> governance
        world -.-> topology
        objects -.-> advanced
    end

    app --> register
    app --> bind
    dispose --> retained --> bind

